diff --git a/release/ontological-priority-of-difference-zenodo-v1/README.md b/release/ontological-priority-of-difference-zenodo-v1/README.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..c52f3f34b122fbb8292b29511e24b380e67502be
--- /dev/null
+++ b/release/ontological-priority-of-difference-zenodo-v1/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,49 @@
+# Zenodo candidate: Ontologischer Vorrang des Unterschieds
+
+Publication ID: `qikvrt-ontological-priority-of-difference-2026-v1`
+
+Target: **CREATE_NEW_ZENODO_RECORD**. The existing related record
+`10.5281/zenodo.21582781` is preserved unchanged.
+
+## Exact scientific subject
+
+> **Am Anfang muss ein Unterschied gewesen sein, denn sonst wäre alles nichts.**
+>
+> **Quod erat demonstrandum, Ingolf Lohmann.**
+
+The publication treats this as an ontological-priority statement, not as a
+first-physical-time or cosmogenesis theorem.
+
+## Intended Zenodo content
+
+The candidate uploads three human-readable articles plus their machine-checkable
+formal context:
+
+1. the scientific article;
+2. the general proof/scope article;
+3. the canonical ontological-origin proof;
+4. the Lean universal-ontology core;
+5. the Lean axiom-audit source;
+6. the formal claim registry;
+7. the publication-specific claim matrix and source/evidence bindings;
+8. citation and license material;
+9. after current-head validation, the v2 machine-proof bundle and
+   prepublication return receipt.
+
+## Fail-closed state
+
+This directory is a prepublication candidate. It is deliberately not executable
+by the generic Zenodo publisher until all of the following are true on the same
+successor subject:
+
+- the current exact HEAD/TREE is bound;
+- the 35-theorem core and 74-constant extended audit have actually executed;
+- the three ontological-origin constants appear in the current kernel receipt;
+- the exact candidate bytes have been returned to Ingolf Lohmann;
+- the canonical candidate-bound natural-person authorization event exists;
+- the final v2 manifest binds that authorization and proof bundle;
+- a valid Zenodo credential is available;
+- public DOI/file redownload succeeds byte-for-byte after publication.
+
+No prior receipt is transferred across a subject mutation.
+`PREDECESSOR_EVIDENCE_TRANSFER=false`.
